+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value   |
+| ------ | ------- |
+| Issue  | #37     |
+| Status | Shipped |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates the input it receives against the tool's declared `inputSchema` before invoking the executor. A call whose input does not satisfy the schema returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the failing constraint; the executor is never invoked. Because the failure is a returned value rather than a thrown error, the model receives the rejection as a tool result and can retry within the existing `DEFAULT_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS` budget.
+
+## Validation contract
+
+When `execute` is called with input that is missing a required property, it returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names that property, and the executor is never invoked. ([validated by: returns a ToolResponse naming the missing required field and does not invoke the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L9))
+
+When `execute` is called with a property whose value has the wrong type, it returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` contains the property path but not the offending value, and the executor is never invoked. Rejection messages never echo input values to prevent identifying data from leaking through error text. ([validated by: returns a ToolResponse with the field path in the message but not the offending value when a property has the wrong type](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L32))
+
+A validation failure is returned as a `ToolResponse`, not thrown, so `processMessage` resolves when the model retries with valid input after receiving the rejection as a tool result. ([validated by: feeds the validation failure back to the model as a ToolResponse so processMessage resolves through a rejected tool call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L58))
